      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect. I found the answer.\n\nThe Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through **credential scoping** \u2014 as described in [[credential-scoping]]:\n\nA local secrets loader reads the Anthropic API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it directly into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts. Crucially, the Hub\u0027s own process environment is **never mutated** with the key.\n\nThis architecture means that if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, an attacker cannot leak the credential by simply inspecting the Hub\u0027s environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API.\n\nThe same scoping model also applies to the Query agent: it receives the credential the same way, injected into its own environment at spawn, never inherited from or stored in the Hub\u0027s process environment.",
      "input_tokens": 5346,
      "output_tokens": 208
    }
